note bottom of "ores::synthetic::service::feed_controller"
The edges the automated pass draws in this component are
none: it reads data members, and the service's own headers
hold almost none. The one line above that names an edge the
code does not support would be a reader's guess, not the
pass's -- so nothing here contradicts the automated pass.
end note

note bottom of "ores::synthetic::service::app::application"
The run() coroutine is the component's start-up contract,
and the order in it is load-bearing: the JetStream streams
must exist before the first feed publishes (js_publish to a
subject with no matching stream throws), the controller must
exist before the registrar's lambdas capture it, and the
controller must be shut down after the NATS I/O loop stops
so no handler callback races the shutdown.
end note

